// Practice quiz: Reading CSV and JSON files with generators
// Formative, low-stakes retention practice. First draft, not reviewed. Titles name the objective id each item practises.

$CATEGORY: python/data-pipelines/reading-csv-and-json-files-with-generators

::o1 csv row type::csv.DictReader reads a line id,qty with values 1,2. What is the type of row["qty"]? {
~int #Not quite. No inference happens; every value arrives as a string.
~float #Not quite. No numeric conversion happens at all.
~bytes #Not quite. A file opened in text mode gives decoded strings.
=str #Correct. The csv module does not convert values; conversion is your job.
}

::o1 encoding::Why name encoding\="utf-8" when opening a file in a pipeline? {
~open() raises an error without it #Not quite. open() works without it, using the platform default.
~It makes the file read faster #Not quite. It controls decoding, not speed.
~It lets open() read JSON documents #Not quite. open() knows nothing about JSON; it only decodes text.
=The default encoding depends on the machine, so the same file can decode differently #Correct. Explicit encoding keeps the read repeatable across machines.
}

::o2 json load bound::A function calls json.load(f) and then yields each item of the result. What is true about memory? {
~Only one item is in memory at a time #Not quite. That needs a source read record by record, such as JSON Lines.
~Memory is bounded because the function uses yield #Not quite. yield pauses the function; it does not change what was already loaded.
=The whole document is in memory before the first yield #Correct. json.load parses everything first, so the generator bounds nothing.
~json.load streams one key at a time #Not quite. json.load returns the fully parsed document.
}

::o2 body start::gen \= read_rows(p) has run. When does the first line of the body of read_rows execute? {
=On the first next(gen) or the first pass of a for loop #Correct. The body starts only when a value is requested.
~During the call read_rows(p) #Not quite. The call only creates the generator object.
~When the module is imported #Not quite. Import only defines the function.
~When gen is garbage collected #Not quite. Collection may close a generator but does not start its body.
}

::o3 second pass::A pipeline logs a count by iterating a generator, then loads the same generator into a table. The table ends up empty and no error appears. What happened? {
~The file was closed by the logger #Not quite. The logger does not touch the file; the generator was simply exhausted.
=The count exhausted the generator, so the load saw nothing #Correct. Generators are single-use and a second pass quietly yields nothing.
~The generator rewound but the table rejected the rows #Not quite. Generators cannot rewind.
~StopIteration was swallowed by the database driver #Not quite. The driver received nothing to insert; the cause is the earlier exhaustion.
}
